course: dictionary
lesson: 6343
title: One word, many meanings: mouth
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. The word mouth is a good example. Its first meaning is the opening in your face that you use for eating, speaking and breathing. «Digestion begins in the mouth: teeth chew and saliva softens food.»
explain: Look at the words around mouth to find its meaning. «The black mamba opens its inky black mouth» is about an animal's face. «The mouth of a cave» is about an opening or entrance, and «the river mouth» is the place where a river ends in the sea. The clues show which meaning is right.
explain: Mouth can also be a verb. To mouth words means to make the shape of them with your lips, but without any sound. Try it in a mirror. When you read, check which meaning fits by swapping your idea into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
fact: Mouth is a noun (plural: mouths) and a verb (mouths, mouthed).
fact: The mouth is the opening in the face for eating, speaking and breathing.
fact: A cave has a mouth too: it is the opening where you go in.
fact: A river's mouth is the place where the river flows into the sea.
fact: «Keep your mouth shut» means don't say anything. «Mouth-watering» means food that looks or smells very tasty.
exercise: «Picture a dentist's X-ray of a seven-year-old: the baby teeth sit in the mouth.» Where do the baby teeth sit? | In the feet | *In the mouth | In the ears | On the roof of a shelf
exercise: «Snakes smell with their forked tongue, which carries scent to a special organ in the roof of the mouth.» What does the forked tongue carry? | Food | Sound | Water | *Scent
exercise: What does mouth mean in «the river mouth»? | The top of a hill | *The place where a river flows into the sea | A bridge over the water | A kind of fish
test: Science lesson: «Digestion begins in the mouth: teeth chew and saliva softens food.» Where does digestion begin? | *In the mouth | In the stomach | In the ears | In the feet
test: Grandad says, «Keep your mouth shut about the surprise.» What does «keep your mouth shut» mean? | Open wide and sing loudly | *Don't say anything | Eat your dinner quickly | Shout for help
exam: Which of these is a verb use of mouth? | *To make the shape of words with your lips, without sound | An entrance to a cave | The opening in your face for eating | The place where a river ends
